  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule)\n(section) SECTION 1 (ratifies S.C. Constitution Art. II, Sec. 4 as amended by Joint Resolution 1126 of 2024)\n(quote) Section 4. Only a citizen of the United States and of this State of the age of eighteen and upwards who is properly registered is entitled to vote as provided by law.\n(other) SECTION 1 also recites that the amendment was submitted at the 2024 General Election and received a favorable vote, and declares it part of the Constitution.\n(other) version: 2025-04-16_Introduced: ratification of the citizens-only voter-qualification amendment (from S 1126 of 2024); no slots a-d.\n(other) version: 2025-04-16_Amended: UNREADABLE (error page). The House Judiciary amendment (reported 2026-04-29) is not seen in it.\n(other) version: zz-final_ratified: Act No. 245 as ratified 2026-05-14 (R 143). Its operative words are identical to the introduced version: same recital about Joint Resolution 1126 of 2024 and the same Section 4 text. Slots a-d: none.\n(other) note: Furthest version is the ratified Act No. 245 (R 143, ratified 2026-05-14, no signature required, effective 05/16/26), read from zz-final_ratified. Its words match the introduced text, so the House committee amendment did not change the operative constitutional wording; what the amendment changed is not visible (the amended file is an error page). Senate vote 2025-04-24 was on the introduced text. The House vote 2026-05-05 was on the bill as amended by House Judiciary; the enrolled text that followed (read third time 05-06) is the ratified act, so the citizens-only wording was in the voted bill, but the exact amended print is not saved.\n(note) Off this topic: the bill sets no ID or citizenship-proof rule.",
